layout: base.njk
title: How it works
permalink: /how-it-works/
steps:
  - ["April – May", "The evidence gate", "Advisers compile candidates only from formal findings by recognized bodies: ICC arrest warrants and indictments, UN commissions of inquiry, and court judgments. A candidate without at least one such finding goes no further, however grave the acts."]
  - ["May – June", "Scoring", "Each adviser scores every remaining candidate from 1 to 5 on four equally weighted factors: gravity, personal responsibility, impunity and recency. Advisers with any tie to a candidate step aside."]
  - ["By 31 July", "Discussion and vote", "The scores open the discussion; they do not decide it. All advisers vote. Individual scores and votes stay sealed for 50 years; the published dossier says which factors decided the award."]
  - ["By 31 August", "Notice and right of response", "The honoree receives written notice and the full dossier, and has 30 days to respond. If the response shows a factual error, the award can be corrected or withheld. Candidates who are not chosen are never contacted."]
  - ["1 October", "Announcement", "The citation, the full evidence dossier and the honoree's unedited response are published together, on the anniversary of the 1946 Nuremberg judgment."]
safeguards:
  - ["Attributed wording", "Every claim is attributed to its source. A citation never declares anyone guilty."]
  - ["Legal review", "A lawyer reviews each citation and dossier before it is announced."]
  - ["Neutrality", "The same standard applies to allies and adversaries of every government."]
  - ["No incitement", "Nothing in the Censure suggests violence. Any threat made in its name is condemned."]
forms:
  - ["/scoring-sheet/", "Adviser scoring sheet", "Blank form. Completed sheets are sealed."]
  - ["/formats-dossier-indictment/", "Evidence dossier and Indictment formats", "With the wording rules every award follows."]
